6|0@PuzzleAndDragons^1440123833#cua8cv6:CardboardOverlord$:They're easily recognizable if you know what you're looking for. There's also more or less some deductive reasoning involved, based on meta and team compositions. There are only so many Wood leads you'd be running right now in Japan, and the only one who's got that distinctive slick black hair on top is Gon. GZL and Vishnu both have very recognizable headgear, and Liu Bei is such a staple that most people recognize the white hair. The only one you might have real difficulty recognizing is the one that's glared out by the green spark, but with it being next to the other Liu Bei it's also not hard to recognize. It's all about familiarity.
3|0@PuzzleAndDragons^1440117925#cua55wm:viconius$:Heh, you're getting some snark because of the optimal subs in the picture, but you're right that Gon really is very strong and trivializes quite high level content (mainly mythical descends). The "Problem" (if that's what you want to call it) is he can clear such content way, way easier than an easy to use lead like Ronia making him a go to lead for descend farming. And his conditional skill isn't really conditional at all, because it's up from floor 1 until you get hit, you have a built in delay to get back to 100% after getting hit, and being sub-50% still gives you as many HP as teams without a leader skill HP boost. The only reason he wont get Ronia levels of "too easy don't use" hate is because he's a rare JP only collab card. P. S. I love my Gon and use him quite regularly. Brainless Hera-Sowilo farming during 10x descends? Yes please! 
